<title>UK: Courtaulds slips again on patent ruling.</title>
<headline>Courtaulds slips again on patent ruling.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in chemicals group Courtaulds Plc slipped again on Tuesday following Monday's news of a setback in its battle with Austrian fibres producer Lenzing AG in a patent dispute.</p>
<p>Lenzing said yesterday that a U.S. court in Washington had decided in its favour in its Lyocell patent dispute with Courtaulds and confirmed Lenzing's patent in the United States.</p>
<p>The Federal Court of Appeal reversed a summary decision by the New York District Court in November 1995, which ruled the patent invalid for not disclosing the &quot;best mode&quot; of invention.</p>
<p>Shares in Courtaulds were trading 14 pence lower at 293-1/2 pence by early afternoon in volume of over 1-1/2 million.</p>
<p>The shares lost seven pence on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The patent news has produced a couple of sellers,&quot; commented one trader.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
